  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Why Modules Exist",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Module, Defined",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Module = packages versioned and released as one unit",
            "Rooted at the directory holding `go.mod`",
            "Unit of versioning, dependency and distribution",
            "Not the unit of compilation — packages still are"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The GOPATH Years"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "All code lived under `$GOPATH/src/<import path>`",
            "One global version per dependency, machine-wide",
            "No version records — `go get` always fetched master",
            "So builds were never reproducible twice"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "`dep`, `glide`, `godep`, `govendor` were community band-aids. Modules arrived in Go 1.11 and became the default in 1.16, replacing all of them."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Path Arithmetic"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Piece",
            "Value"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "module path",
              "`example.com/m`"
            ],
            [
              "subdirectory",
              "`util`"
            ],
            [
              "import path",
              "`example.com/m/util`"
            ],
            [
              "v2 or later",
              "`example.com/m/v2`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Module path = import prefix for every package inside",
            "Must be resolvable: a URL, or private via `GOPRIVATE`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "go mod init example.com/m  # writes go.mod",
            "go mod init                # infers the path",
            "# from the VCS remote or old vendor config"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "GOPATH Today"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Code lives anywhere on disk — modules are self-contained",
            "`$GOPATH/pkg/mod` holds the module cache",
            "`$GOPATH/bin` holds binaries from `go install`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "GO111MODULE",
          "items": [
            "`on` — the default since Go 1.16",
            "`off` — legacy GOPATH mode",
            "`auto` — module mode only inside a module tree"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flowchart",
          "spec": {
            "title": "repo/",
            "rows": [
              [
                "n0"
              ],
              [
                "b0",
                "b1",
                "b2"
              ],
              [
                "c0_0",
                "c0_1"
              ],
              [
                "c1_0"
              ],
              [
                "c2_0"
              ]
            ],
            "nodes": {
              "n0": {
                "text": "repo/",
                "shape": "diamond"
              },
              "b0": {
                "text": "go.mod"
              },
